        "description": "Absence of known pathogenic mutations in LIS1, DCX, or other lissencephaly-associated genes",
        "category": "major",
        "requiredForDiagnosis": true
      },
      {
        "id": "absence-other-malformations",
        "description": "No evidence of other brain malformations or systemic anomalies",
        "category": "supportive",
        "requiredForDiagnosis": false
      }
    ],
    "minimumForDiagnosis": "Presence of characteristic MRI findings plus clinical neurological features and exclusion of known genetic mutations",
    "notes": "Genetic testing is essential to exclude known causative mutations; diagnosis is primarily radiological and clinical."
